quick-post rj2ep84 rj2ep89" role="article"><a aria-label="What if your 14-inch laptop literally stretched to become a 17-inch Netflix machine?" class="rj2ep88" href="/tech/990634/lenovo-project-swan"></a><div class="rj2ep81"><div class="rj2ep87"><div class="_1jiz7rn0 _1jiz7rn1"><div class="_1jiz7rn7"><img alt="Sean Hollister" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" width="34" height="34" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="_4aoxp34" style="color:transparent" srcSet="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/Sean_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/Sean_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96 2x" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/Sean_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96"/></div><div class="_1jiz7rn2 _1jiz7rn3"><span class="_1jiz7rn6">Sean Hollister</span><span class="duet--article--timestamp g4xafw2 g4xafw0 _19wv7tc5 _1jiz7rna"><time dateTime="2026-09-06T13:06:00+00:00">Sep 6</time></span></div></div><div class="_4ine551 _4ine550"><div class="_4ine554">What if your 14-inch laptop literally stretched to become a 17-inch Netflix machine?</div><div class="_1y5ugvbf _1y5ugvb0"><p class="duet--article--dangerously-set-cms-markup duet--article--standard-paragraph _1044qizi _18mzr4b1 _18mzr4b0 _19wv7tc1"><a href="/tech/989477/lenovo-thinkbook-project-swan-concept-laptop-14-17-rollable-ifa-announcement">Lenovo’s Project Swan</a> has a screen that literally unrolls. The prototype could use better speakers and some weight balancing, but I love watching it in motion!</p></div></div><div class="_1p001ee0"><div class="_1y5ugvb1"><div class="ejz0tzd"></div></div></div></div><div class="dq5wa40"><span class="dq5wa41"></span><span class="_1044qizr"></span><span class="dq5wa42"><div class="_1jiz7rnb dq5wa43"><button aria-label="Copy link"><svg class="_